{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -C 3 '30.day|duration|endTime|sale end|sale-end|sale interval' DESIGN.md WORKSPACE.md; nl -ba packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol | sed -n '409,435p'; nl -ba packages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol | sed -n '36,56p'\"","aggregated_output":"DESIGN.md-1-# Clean design specification\nDESIGN.md:2:Ethereum NFT raffle; immutable factory, ERC-1167 clones with immutable implementation. One entry costs 1,000,000 units of canonical six-decimal USDC. One purchase mints a transferable ERC721 ticket representing a contiguous inclusive range. Exactly one ERC721 prize is escrowed atomically at creation. Reserve met awards NFT and 95% sponsor / 5% treasury. Reserve missed awards 80% gross to winner, 15% sponsor, 5% treasury. Refund outcome pays 100% per entry and returns prize. Rounding is floor on aggregate protocol fee; remainder must be allocated without loss. No administrator, mutable configuration or upgrade. Request window [sale end, end+2days); callback accepted strictly before request timestamp+2days. Refunds open at deadline. Callback records result only. Settlement is permissionless, storage-only; redemption requires current ticket owner, burns claim atomically, and must revert all effects on delivery failure. Sponsor and treasury can claim independently after settlement. Never move assets between raffle clones. Quote token and Chainlink wrapper are trusted canonical dependencies; arbitrary prize contracts and ticket recipients are untrusted. Frontend discovery is advisory; transaction decisions must reread current chain state.\nDESIGN.md-3-\nDESIGN.md-4-This specification was composed before scanner results and historical findings. Source, not design prose, determines actual behavior. No tests, audit history, accepted-risk lists or scanner results are provided.\n   409\t    /// @notice Accepts only the exact configured prize deposited by the factory for the sponsor.\n   410\t    /// @dev Unrelated NFTs forced here with unsafe `transferFrom` remain outside protocol accounting and cannot be\n   411\t    ///      rescued.\n   412\t    /// @param operator ERC-721 transfer operator, which must be the canonical factory.\n   413\t    /// @param from Previous owner, which must be the configured sponsor.\n   414\t    /// @param tokenId Transferred token ID, which must match the configured prize.\n   415\t    /// @return selector ERC-721 receiver acceptance selector.\n   416\t    function onERC721Received(address operator, address from, uint256 tokenId, bytes calldata)\n   417\t        external\n   418\t        override\n   419\t        returns (bytes4 selector)\n   420\t    {\n   421\t        if (\n   422\t            status != Status.AwaitingPrize || msg.sender != address(prizeToken) || tokenId != prizeTokenId\n   423\t                || from != sponsor || operator != factory\n   424\t        ) {\n   425\t            revert UnexpectedPrize(msg.sender, tokenId, from, operator);\n   426\t        }\n   427\t\n   428\t        status = Status.Active;\n   429\t        emit PrizeDeposited(msg.sender, tokenId, from);\n   430\t        selector = IERC721Receiver.onERC721Received.selector;\n   431\t    }\n   432\t\n   433\t    // Public view and pure functions\n   434\t\n   435\t    /// @inheritdoc IRaffle\n    36\t    /// @notice Complete clone-specific configuration supplied once by the canonical factory.\n    37\t    /// @param sponsor Prize depositor and empty-raffle cancellation authority.\n    38\t    /// @param sponsorRecipient Immutable recipient of sponsor quote proceeds and any returned prize.\n    39\t    /// @param protocolTreasury Immutable recipient of protocol fees.\n    40\t    /// @param prizeToken Standards-compliant ERC-721 prize contract.\n    41\t    /// @param prizeTokenId Token ID of the prize escrowed by this raffle.\n    42\t    /// @param raffleId One-based canonical factory identifier for this raffle.\n    43\t    /// @param reserveEntries Global raw entry-count threshold selecting the NFT outcome when met or exceeded.\n    44\t    /// @param endTime Unix timestamp, in seconds, at which entry sales end exclusively.\n    45\t    struct RaffleInitParams {\n    46\t        address sponsor;\n    47\t        address sponsorRecipient;\n    48\t        address protocolTreasury;\n    49\t        address prizeToken;\n    50\t        uint256 prizeTokenId;\n    51\t        uint256 raffleId;\n    52\t        uint128 reserveEntries;\n    53\t        uint64 endTime;\n    54\t    }\n    55\t\n    56\t    // Events\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"_kritt_extractor_helper\":true,\"stub\":true,\"stub_explanation\":\"No supported vulnerability found. The factory checks that endTime is future before subtracting in uint256, then rejects durations exceeding the immutable 30-day limit before deployment, registration, or escrow. Earlier validation cannot mutate state through its external view call, and the revert rolls back the reentrancy guard update. No sponsor-reachable bypass was identified.\",\"results\":[]}"}}
